<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Germany and Central Europe</p><h1 class="st-title">Free State of Mecklenburg</h1><p class="st-meta">1934 CE – 1952 CE · capital Schwerin</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Mecklenburg reunited by the Nazis in 1934, which after 1945 became a Land of the Soviet zone and the GDR until its abolition in 1952.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>On 1 January 1934 a Reich law merged the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/free-state-of-mecklenburg-schwerin">Free State of Mecklenburg-Schwerin</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/free-state-of-mecklenburg-strelitz">Free State of Mecklenburg-Strelitz</a> into a single Land of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/lordship-of-mecklenburg">Mecklenburg</a>, with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-schwerin">Schwerin</a> as capital, ending the division that dated from 1701.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nazi-party">Nazis</a> the state was run by Reich governor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/friedrich-hildebrandt">Friedrich Hildebrandt</a>. Rostock's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/heinkel">Heinkel</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arado-flugzeugwerke">Arado</a> aircraft works made it a target of Allied bombing. In 1945 it was occupied by Soviet and British forces and placed in the Soviet zone, gaining western <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/duchy-of-pomerania">Pomerania</a> and receiving many expellees. A land reform in 1945 broke up the large estates.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Known as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mecklenburg-vorpommern">Mecklenburg-Vorpommern</a> until 1947, the Land became part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-germany">German Democratic Republic</a> in 1949. In 1952 it was divided into the districts of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/lordship-of-rostock">Rostock</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-schwerin">Schwerin</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/neubrandenburg">Neubrandenburg</a>; the state was re-established in 1990 as Mecklenburg-Vorpommern.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="republic, 1934 CE – 1952 CE"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 38 L50 20 L80 38 Z"/><path d="M24 42 H76 M24 80 H76"/><path d="M30 44 V78 M43 44 V78 M57 44 V78 M70 44 V78"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">republic</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Germany and Central Europe</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:98.19%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1934 CE – 1952 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Schwerin</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Friedrich Hildebrandt</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Lutheranism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>German, Low German</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/germany">Germany</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Land Mecklenburg</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1943&amp;focus=free-state-of-mecklenburg" aria-label="Free State of Mecklenburg on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4934 335 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Free State of Mecklenburg lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5254 591L5254 591M5254 591L5291 598M5254 591L5300 622"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5254 591h0M5291 598h0M5300 622h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5254 591h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5254 591h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Schwerin. <a href="/atlas?year=1943&amp;focus=free-state-of-mecklenburg">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
